{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011qmdchfx4Het64ZuBpxrew","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→\"\"\"AudioResult value object for domain layer.\n     2→\n     3→Result of audio processing operations.\n     4→\"\"\"\n     5→\n     6→from dataclasses import dataclass\n     7→from datetime import UTC, datetime\n     8→from pathlib import Path\n     9→\n    10→\n    11→@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\n    12→class AudioResult:\n    13→    \"\"\"Value object representing the result of audio processing.\n    14→\n    15→    This is an immutable value object containing metadata about\n    16→    processed audio output.\n    17→\n    18→    Attributes:\n    19→        output_path: Path to the processed audio file\n    20→        duration_seconds: Duration of the audio in seconds\n    21→        sample_rate: Sample rate of the output audio in Hz\n    22→        peak_dbfs: Peak level in dB relative to full scale\n    23→        lufs_integrated: Integrated loudness in LUFS (EBU R128)\n    24→        processing_time_seconds: Time taken to process in seconds\n    25→        processed_at: Timestamp when processing completed\n    26→    \"\"\"\n    27→\n    28→    output_path: Path\n    29→    duration_seconds: float\n    30→    sample_rate: int\n    31→    peak_dbfs: float\n    32→    lufs_integrated: float\n    33→    processing_time_seconds: float\n    34→    processed_at: datetime\n    35→\n    36→    @classmethod\n    37→    def create(\n    38→        cls,\n    39→        output_path: Path,\n    40→        duration_seconds: float,\n    41→        sample_rate: int,\n    42→        peak_dbfs: float,\n    43→        lufs_integrated: float,\n    44→        processing_time_seconds: float,\n    45→    ) -> \"AudioResult\":\n    46→        \"\"\"Create an AudioResult with the current timestamp.\n    47→\n    48→        Args:\n    49→            output_path: Path to the processed audio file\n    50→            duration_seconds: Duration of the audio in seconds\n    51→            sample_rate: Sample rate of the output audio in Hz\n    52→            peak_dbfs: Peak level in dB relative to full scale\n    53→            lufs_integrated: Integrated loudness in LUFS\n    54→            processing_time_seconds: Time taken to process in seconds\n    55→\n    56→        Returns:\n    57→            A new AudioResult instance with processed_at set to now\n    58→        \"\"\"\n    59→        return cls(\n    60→            output_path=output_path,\n    61→            duration_seconds=duration_seconds,\n    62→            sample_rate=sample_rate,\n    63→            peak_dbfs=peak_dbfs,\n    64→            lufs_integrated=lufs_integrated,\n    65→            processing_time_seconds=processing_time_seconds,\n    66→            processed_at=datetime.now(UTC),\n    67→        )\n    68→\n    69→    def is_clipping(self, threshold_dbfs: float = -0.1) -> bool:\n    70→        \"\"\"Check if the audio is clipping based on peak level.\n    71→\n    72→        Args:\n    73→            threshold_dbfs: Threshold in dBFS above which audio is considered\n    74→                clipping. Default is -0.1 dBFS.\n    75→\n    76→        Returns:\n    77→            True if peak_dbfs is above the threshold, False otherwise\n    78→        \"\"\"\n    79→        return self.peak_dbfs > threshold_dbfs\n    80→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f68c697a-3ba6-4786-9052-dcd080c87723","uuid":"7e95a9c2-8132-4dbb-94dd-ba502e9bcb77","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"libs/core/src/core/domain/value_objects/audio_result.py","content":"\"\"\"AudioResult value object for domain layer.\n\nResult of audio processing operations.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom datetime import UTC, datetime\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass AudioResult:\n    \"\"\"Value object representing the result of audio processing.\n\n    This is an immutable value object containing metadata about\n    processed audio output.\n\n    Attributes:\n        output_path: Path to the processed audio file\n        duration_seconds: Duration of the audio in seconds\n        sample_rate: Sample rate of the output audio in Hz\n        peak_dbfs: Peak level in dB relative to full scale\n        lufs_integrated: Integrated loudness in LUFS (EBU R128)\n        processing_time_seconds: Time taken to process in seconds\n        processed_at: Timestamp when processing completed\n    \"\"\"\n\n    output_path: Path\n    duration_seconds: float\n    sample_rate: int\n    peak_dbfs: float\n    lufs_integrated: float\n    processing_time_seconds: float\n    processed_at: datetime\n\n    @classmethod\n    def create(\n        cls,\n        output_path: Path,\n        duration_seconds: float,\n        sample_rate: int,\n        peak_dbfs: float,\n        lufs_integrated: float,\n        processing_time_seconds: float,\n    ) -> \"AudioResult\":\n        \"\"\"Create an AudioResult with the current timestamp.\n\n        Args:\n            output_path: Path to the processed audio file\n            duration_seconds: Duration of the audio in seconds\n            sample_rate: Sample rate of the output audio in Hz\n            peak_dbfs: Peak level in dB relative to full scale\n            lufs_integrated: Integrated loudness in LUFS\n            processing_time_seconds: Time taken to process in seconds\n\n        Returns:\n            A new AudioResult instance with processed_at set to now\n        \"\"\"\n        return cls(\n            output_path=output_path,\n            duration_seconds=duration_seconds,\n            sample_rate=sample_rate,\n            peak_dbfs=peak_dbfs,\n            lufs_integrated=lufs_integrated,\n            processing_time_seconds=processing_time_seconds,\n            processed_at=datetime.now(UTC),\n        )\n\n    def is_clipping(self, threshold_dbfs: float = -0.1) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Check if the audio is clipping based on peak level.\n\n        Args:\n            threshold_dbfs: Threshold in dBFS above which audio is considered\n                clipping. Default is -0.1 dBFS.\n\n        Returns:\n            True if peak_dbfs is above the threshold, False otherwise\n        \"\"\"\n        return self.peak_dbfs > threshold_dbfs\n","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":80}}}
